SAMStat 2.5.0 - quality control for SAM/BAM/CRAM and FASTA/FASTQ files

Usage: samstat [options] <file|-> [file ...]

  -d, --dir DIR      write reports to DIR (created if missing) [next to input]
  -p, --peek N       analyse only the first N reads (not random) [all]
  -t, --threads N    total threads, 1-64, at most the number of CPUs [4]
      --json         also write <input>.samstat.json
      --multiqc      also write MultiQC files <input>.samstat_*_mqc.json
      --verbose      debug output
  -h, --help / -v, --version

Input type (SAM, BAM, CRAM, FASTA or FASTQ, plain or gzip) is detected from the
content. CRAM needs its reference, found through REF_PATH or REF_CACHE (no
network). A file name of - reads standard input (once); its reports are
named stdin.samstat.*.
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 one or more inputs failed, 2 usage error (bad option,
-d DIR not writable, colliding report names; nothing is read).

Examples:
  samstat sample.bam
  samstat -d qc/ run/*.bam run/*.fastq.gz

